<http://data.silknow.org/object/3cac3258-9e53-325e-b8c7-a5d5b40862d7>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Saddle cloth or mat. Silk and gold thread brocade cloth (Kinkhab), Ahmedabad, Gujarat, early 19th century"@en , "SADDLE CLOTH: Silk and gold thread brocade cloth (Kinkhab), padded, lined and fringed with gold-thread tassels. Ahmedabad, Gujarat. First half of the 19th century. [Nehru Gallery, 2001]"@en , "A rectangular saddle-cloth or small mat, of silk and gold thread brocade cloth (kinkhab), padded, lined and fringed with gold-thread tassels. The field has a trellis design made up of flowers and leaves; three outer borders have floral meander patterns."@en , "According to the acquisition records of the India Museum, to which this saddle-cloth or small carpet belonged before coming to the South Kensington Museum in 1879, this piece  was formerly in the collection of a 'General Malcolm', presumably Sir John Malcolm (1769-1833) who was Governor of Bombay from 1827-30. A saddle-cloth identical to this one was exhibited at the Great Exhibition in 1851, and attracted the admiration of Owen Jones for its design and harmony of colours."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/c50dc153-497d-3541-898b-2fb7217d7b34> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/22017694-2b14-3e13-8aff-ab4e2f8c8e66> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/6fef077a-fbe4-385d-bc42-2098a6c6c98f> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/e1dc6708-0466-3ce9-97c1-029d19385e0d> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "According to the acquisition records of the India Museum, to which this saddle-cloth or small carpet belonged before coming to the South Kensington Museum in 1879, this piece  was formerly in the collection of a 'General Malcolm', presumably Sir John Malcolm (1769-1833) who was Governor of Bombay from 1827-30. A saddle-cloth identical to this one was exhibited at the Great Exhibition in 1851, and attracted the admiration of Owen Jones for its design and harmony of colours."@en , "Saddle cloth or mat. Silk and gold thread brocade cloth (Kinkhab), Ahmedabad, Gujarat, early 19th century"@en , "A rectangular saddle-cloth or small mat, of silk and gold thread brocade cloth (kinkhab), padded, lined and fringed with gold-thread tassels. The field has a trellis design made up of flowers and leaves; three outer borders have floral meander patterns."@en , "SADDLE CLOTH: Silk and gold thread brocade cloth (Kinkhab), padded, lined and fringed with gold-thread tassels. Ahmedabad, Gujarat. First half of the 19th century. [Nehru Gallery, 2001]"@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/3cac3258-9e53-325e-b8c7-a5d5b40862d7/dimension/2> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/3cac3258-9e53-325e-b8c7-a5d5b40862d7/dimension/1> ;
        dc:identifier                  "0683(IS)" ;
